  "reconstruction": {
    "scope": "Specific Peter Mokaba Stadium: native oval bowl/open central floor, one completed western side canopy with closed pale skins/underside rafters and green arched girder, four rounded concrete circulation trunks/open helical ramp approximations with white branches on the two canopy-supporting western cores, warm orange/sand/brown two-tier seating set inside the corner circulation cores/radial aisles/central hospitality band, recessed concrete service facade/closed entries, neutral football field/markings/goals and independently supported end boards/light frames. Five existing shared concrete/paint/standing-seam/window-grid/canvas graphs. Opposite long stand and both ends remain uncovered. No proposed full roof, old neighboring stadium, whole sports campus/parking slab, copied crowd/event artwork or furnished service interior.",
    "identityBasis": "Retained exact-QID OSMrelation952159 identifies the individual stadium; standard PMTiles parent52776559085407 supplies its oval shell/central opening. Own anchor[29.468830124556625,-23.924809767142666]/heading0/native east-south, internal X[0.2290394288305648,-0.9734171459559199]/Z[0.9734171459559199,0.2290394288305648] follows the131.210855x84.671333m native opening. The whole body follows its actual irregular ring, rather than stretching the field to the wider311.874x248.48m stadium envelope. Western service-side extensions and ordinary canopy/bowl photographs fix the single-side coverage; signed frontage and fine core/row/portal positions retain20degree/2m visualization uncertainty. Independent old stadium, nearby utilities and parking remain native.",
    "heightBasis": "No qualified architectural heights are retained. Working upper seating28m, single canopy37..41.4m with175m nominal span, green arch approximately39..52.5m, circular trunk31.4m/ramp22.3m and lower/service bands are picture-led visual allocations. Canopy span/width and four core centers are unmeasured reconstruction estimates inside the mapped bowl, not engineering dimensions. Ramp turns/slopes/landings/rails, detailed branch/rafter inventory and fine20degree/2m facing are approximate; no access/structural certification or concealed interior claim. AFL ordinary pictures show one completed canopy; unbuilt full-ring/other-side roof is excluded.105x68m neutral football configuration differs from the rugby events in the reference photos; temporary H-posts/crowd/sponsors are excluded. Later changes and current seat inventory are unverified.",
    "terrainBasis": "Standard6m Mapzen ground remains unmodified; raw anchor sample defines modelY0 and each corner core stores its own sampled native contact datum. Stadium perimeter relative range-3.3578598948392937..3.873421371810082m; core contacts/closed footings and a bounded opening within90percent of the bowl/common supported floor handle coarse terrain intrusion. The opening is not a surveyed real excavation. Original samples/outside terrain/roads/water and every unrelated building remain intact; only the owned stadium shell is replaced. Failure/unload restore original ground. No external whole-site platform, ground flattening or water cutout.",
